Third-party runtime

The portable Windows bundle redistributes the Electron runtime
(https://www.electronjs.org), Copyright (c) OpenJS Foundation and other
contributors, licensed under the MIT License. Its license file is shipped
alongside the binary in the release archive as `LICENSE.electron.txt`.

This repository contains no vendored third-party source code. All application
code under `main.js`, `renderer/`, and the `*.js` logic modules is original
work licensed under the terms above.

Relationship to Hermes

This project is an independent community project. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or distributed as part of the Hermes project. It does not copy or
redistribute Hermes source code; it only invokes the locally installed
`hermes` command line interface at runtime.
